{
  "$schema": "https://turbo.build/schema.json",
  "extends": ["//"],
  // WHY THIS FILE EXISTS — the same defect `deploy/airgap/turbo.json` documents, found in this
  // package while hardening the pin gate against commented-out pins (M21.7). A census whose SUBJECT
  // lives outside its own package is invisible to turbo's default (package-scoped) input hashing,
  // so the gate is replayed from cache instead of run.
  //
  // MEASURED 2026-08-17, before this file existed: `pin.test.ts` is the drift gate that decides
  // WHICH SCANNER BINARY the runner image is built FROM. Editing `apps/runner-scan/Dockerfile`'s
  // `ARG TRIVY_IMAGE=` to an all-zeros digest — an unvetted image, the exact thing the gate exists
  // to refuse — and re-running `turbo run test --filter=@scp/plugin-managed-scan` reported
  // `>>> FULL TURBO`, 5/5 cached, green. Nothing in this package had changed, so nothing ran. A
  // cache hit on the very input a test is about is the same defect as a test that never asserts,
  // and it would have quietly undone the anchoring fix that landed alongside this file.
  //
  // `$TURBO_ROOT$` (turbo 2.1+) is what makes an out-of-package input expressible.
  //
  // DELIBERATELY WIDE, and honest about it: `scanner-containment.test.ts` sweeps `git ls-files`
  // across every tracked file under apps/, packages/, deploy/, scripts/ and tools/, because the
  // invariant it guards ("a scanner exists ONLY in apps/runner-scan") is a property of the WHOLE
  // repo — a `RUN dnf install openscap-scanner` added anywhere is what it is looking for. Narrowing
  // these inputs to make the cache hit more often would narrow the sweep to match, which is how the
  // gate gets weakened until it passes vacuously. This package's suite runs in about a second; the
  // cache is not worth the hole.
  "tasks": {
    "test": {
      "dependsOn": ["build"],
      "inputs": [
        "$TURBO_DEFAULT$",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/apps/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/packages/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/deploy/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/scripts/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/tools/**",
        "$TURBO_ROOT$/Dockerfile"
      ]
    }
  }
}
